Mutation
- [N33] Node-level mutation: element=action(n10,"credit card approved and inventory in stock?"); source=i7:If the credit card is approved and there is inventory in stock, they can continue with the process. -> i8:However, if the credit card is denied or there is no inventory in stock, the transaction will end.; reason=The source describes a single joint condition checking both credit card status and inventory availability. The model fractures this into separate nodes, converts the condition into a question/state label, and completely omits the inventory requirement from the guards, retaining only credit card approval/denial logic. This alters the core business rule.
